# vault/.gitignore
# Protects the outer vault git repository.
# NEVER commit secrets, private notes, or the nested Project/ repo here.
# See vault/Security/ for the full secret-handling policy.

# ── Nested repo ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Project/ is its own git repository with independent versioning and nightly
# backup. Excluding its CONTENTS here prevents double-tracking, but the seed
# README.md must still ship as scaffold. A bare `Project/` would exclude the
# dir outright and defeat the root .gitignore's `!vault/Project/README.md`.
Project/*
!Project/README.md

# ── Private / sensitive sections ────────────────────────────────────────────
# Keep Security/README.md and policy docs TRACKED (they contain no secrets).
# Only exclude an explicitly-private subfolder for sensitive notes.
Security/private/
.private/

# ── Secrets — never commit (defense in depth) ────────────────────────────────
# Secrets live in the secrets manager, not in markdown files.
# These patterns are a last-resort safety net.
*.env
.env
*.key
*.pem
secrets.*

# ── Obsidian local workspace state ──────────────────────────────────────────
# Workspace layout, recent-files cache, and plugin data are machine-local.
.obsidian/workspace*
.obsidian/cache
.obsidian/plugins/
.trash/

# ── Hindsight sync bookkeeping ──────────────────────────────────────────────
# The sync state file records the last-sync epoch for mtime-incremental logic.
# It is local runtime state, not knowledge.
.hindsight-sync-state
*.syncstate

# ── OS / editor cruft ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.swp
*~
